    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1322-a2">

                <pb facs="1257" n="1091" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg1091"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 – Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">General Pershing to the Adjutant General </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Fort Sam Houston</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-04-28">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 28, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5075. Reference your 6586. Reply to your No. 6449 delayed awaiting word from
                    Chinese Consul General regarding assurances given by Chinese Minister. No word
                    yet received by Chinese Consul from Minister authorizing former to act. Your
                    telegram implies that assurances already given for purpose of accepting
                    employment by military establishment. Situation not so understood by Consul
                    General at Columbus. Latter has strongly recommended to Chinese Minister that
                    Chinese refugees be permitted to accept employment by military establishment and
                    that refugees be sent to San Antonio for that purpose. Have deferred action
                    awaiting reply to his recommendation. Suggest matter be taken up by State
                    Department with view to transfer of refugees from Columbus to San Antonio where
                    they can be given employment. Chinese Minister should assume responsibility for
                    refugee laborers who are discharged for cause or who desert.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Pershing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
